{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets","id":1515745,"title":"W5- Loresheets.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-21T08:20:37-07:00","id":1515745,"title":"W5- Loresheets.","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1121050920218800248/unnamed-1.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1121050920218800248/unnamed-1.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1121050920218800248/unnamed-1.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/609799022873673729/1121050920218800248/unnamed-1.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Oh, dear....the Project Twilight is just...weird unless there are Garou FBI agents now.<br /> <br /> The Umbral one is a collection of things all Garou could do, a Silent Strider/Ivory Lodge Gift, a Glasswalker Gift and a Background...its kinda a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 06-21-2023, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T08:36:45-07:00","id":1515746,"title":"","content":"Well, that's certainly something...<ul><li>Whoever the writer for Ahroun and the Project Twilight Loresheet is, I dread to read more of... whatever that is.</li> <li>The dots for Project Twilight are confusing...So you're working with Project Twilight...? Somehow you've got dirt on a Fed-funded kill-squad...? How does that fit into the worldbuilding of who Garou are in W5...?</li> <li>The Umbral Traveler Loresheet mentions that you need to spend WP to stay in the Umbra or take damage. Great... so now investing in Composure and Resolve during char-gen is a must. You need WP 4 (at least!) or you're in trouble.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T09:31:33-07:00","id":1515751,"title":"","content":"So, you can't go to umbra, can't change to crinos, can't use your powers of garou or you are f*****... where is the fun in this game?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10047_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T09:38:11-07:00","id":1515752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vis\u00e3o-de-\u00c1guia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515751#post1515751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, you can't go to umbra, can't change to crinos, can't use your powers of garou or you are f*****... where is the fun in this game?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal theory at this point is that what the game is going for is to make every Garou/werewolf-related mechanic punishing to some degree. And the takeaway is supposed to be that mundane, human activism is the better route as mechanics enforce the idea that using your powers as a werewolf/Garou always comes with a cost. Whatever you gain using your werewolf/spirit-powers, you will always lose something in the process... or something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:14:07-07:00","id":1515753,"title":"","content":"Man, they crippled Umbral side of Werewolf as well<br /> Actually...<br /> ...where was the first loresheet in H5? Why is W5 has more positive interactions with a Hunter Organization than actual H5 Hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:22:07-07:00","id":1515755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515753#post1515753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, they crippled Umbral side of Werewolf as well<br /> Actually...<br /> ...where was the first loresheet in H5? Why is W5 has more positive interactions with a Hunter Organization than actual H5 Hunters?</div> </div> </div> </div>H5 has a whole sidebar on that (pg 80). The gist of it is that due to the assumed limited understanding of H5 PCs when it comes to the WOD it's assumed your standard-Hunter wouldn't have access to anything like Loresheets... and that's why H5 doesn't have any. Personally, I'd argue a Loresheet similar to the Project Twilight one would've been perfect to integrate hunter-orgs into the game while still insisting that hunter-orgs aren't player-options... but well, it is what it is, I guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:26:41-07:00","id":1515756,"title":"","content":"Okay sooo;<br /> <br /> Staying in Crinos without killing costs WP.<br /> <br /> You need to use WP to stay in the umbra or TAKE AGG DAMAGE!?<br /> <br /> There are TWO important tools made EXTREMELY unpleasant to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:33:07-07:00","id":1515757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515756#post1515756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay sooo;<br /> <br /> Staying in Crinos without killing costs WP.<br /> <br /> You need to use WP to stay in the umbra or TAKE AGG DAMAGE!?<br /> <br /> There are TWO important tools made EXTREMELY unpleasant to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't forget that there are also two categories of Gifts and Rites: One needs you to do a Rage-check, the other... needs you to spend <i>a point of WP</i>. Actually, forget going for WP 4 at character-creation. You need to have at least 5 WP to stomach all of that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:36:06-07:00","id":1515758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515757#post1515757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, don't forget that there are also two categories of Gifts and Rites: One needs you to do a Rage-check, the other... needs you to spend <i>a point of WP</i>. Actually, forget going for WP 4 at character-creation. You need to have at least 5 WP to stomach all of that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you just stay in homid and never enter the umbra. After all, you CLEARLY are getting much more out of working with Project Twilight than entering the umbra at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T10:40:41-07:00","id":1515759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515758#post1515758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or you just stay in homid and never enter the umbra. After all, you CLEARLY are getting much more out of working with Project Twilight than entering the umbra at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Forget the war against the Wyrm, try surviving minimun-wage-labor/gig-work first!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T13:30:04-07:00","id":1515776,"title":"","content":"While the crinos limit has its reasons, as does the umbra one, I feel both are done in such a way that they penalize trying to engage with the setting's core traits. Especially when the Project Twilight example, which should be a much harder thing to deal with, is easier and more rewarding.<br /> <br /> Using a hunter group should be a much more punishing thing than using the umbra, since one is going out of your way to painting a target on your back and the other is part of garou nature. The Hisil in Forsaken is more limited, but it doesn't make you take damage for simply existing in it.<br /> <br /> It doesn't make for something you'd want to engage with, and most players I've met will not waste resources for a maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T14:32:49-07:00","id":1515787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515776#post1515776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the crinos limit has its reasons, as does the umbra one, I feel both are done in such a way that they penalize trying to engage with the setting's core traits. Especially when the Project Twilight example, which should be a much harder thing to deal with, is easier and more rewarding.<br /> <br /> Using a hunter group should be a much more punishing thing than using the umbra, since one is going out of your way to painting a target on your back and the other is part of garou nature. The Hisil in Forsaken is more limited, but it doesn't make you take damage for simply existing in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're probably still inflicting Avatar Storm BS on Garou. Even though that should have been in a different setting... yet not, because it wasn't until very late into W20 that any hint of the Avatar Storm started being a problem for Garou or Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T14:59:54-07:00","id":1515793,"title":"","content":"On a side-note... I just noticed that these Loresheets in the previews are pages 296 and 297 in a section called &quot;Appendix One: Loresheets&quot; and the book is advertised as having 300+ pages. That would then mean in terms of page-count it's in the low 300s. So it's only a dozen pages or so longer than the H5 corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T20:05:38-07:00","id":1515819,"title":"","content":"&quot;The spirits wilds constitute a mystery even to the garou, whose animistic outlook makes them familiar to the spirit world but not strickly of it&quot;<br /> <br /> *Caugh* what is this? It's exactly the opposite! The gaou are, by their half spirit nature, OF the spirit world as much as the material one. They are of it, but not necessarily familiar to it.<br /> <br /> And it's indeed their nature that give them a form of understanding of the umbra, not their animistic outlook, which is a consequence of the former.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The theory that the authors of W5 despise Wta seems to be more and more valid.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit, the twilight project one is indeed also weird. The V5 second inquisition loresheets were all about knowing how to avoid the SI's attention, but this one seems like garou have some interests in snitching to an org dedicated to hunt them.<br /> <br /> If anything, it should have been the reverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 06-21-2023, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T22:50:59-07:00","id":1515823,"title":"","content":"I like Twilight loresheet. Character could use them in the past pointing direction at BSD. It's not that you have physical contact with them, you could be important informer, besides they cover your activities maby against II inquisition (as I see it):<br /> <br /> 1 dot - something that could be used against your pack is missing , maby some evidence of garou existance like photo, that's very fine for me!<br /> <br /> 2 dot - better then first, cause it gives you false witness.<br /> <br /> 3 dot - you are monster, but their monster, one their leash, so you use it in negotiations to require something from them - that is strange but fun<br /> <br /> 4 dot - that is the best dot in my opinion, so you can packe your stuff and disappear before something bad happen - like you have some informant inside the project<br /> <br /> 5 dot - that is very strong, cause you're directing twilight against anyone you want BUT with every consequences<br /> <br /> I wander what is protracted period of time - for me it's about balance between umbra and normal world pressed in game mechanics, So I am very curious about it - how long can you stay in umbra before something would slowly disintegrate your body and maby turn you into spirit totally.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T22:52:35-07:00","id":1515824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515819#post1515819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The spirits wilds constitute a mystery even to the garou, whose animistic outlook makes them familiar to the spirit world but not strickly of it&quot;<br /> <br /> *Caugh* what is this? It's exactly the opposite! The gaou are, by their half spirit nature, OF the spirit world as much as the material one. They are of it, but not necessarily familiar to it.<br /> <br /> And it's indeed their nature that give them a form of understanding of the umbra, not their animistic outlook, which is a consequence of the former.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is the same but it's phrased differently to, I guess, emphasize that Garou in W5 aren't familiar with spirits and the Umbra. The phrasing you get in the introduction is: &quot;Werewolves belong to multiple worlds \u2014 spirit and flesh, wolf and human \u2014 but are wholly accepted by none\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> edit, the twilight project one is indeed also weird. The V5 second inquisition loresheets were all about knowing how to avoid the SI's attention, but this one seems like garou have some interests in snitching to an org dedicated to hunt them.<br /> <br /> If anything, it should have been the reverse.\u200b </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Stolen Valor&quot;-one is especially weird where Project Twilight killed a Garou and your character claims instead to have been responsible for the death. Even more so because first, it says you gain a three-die-bonus to social tests because of the achievement but then it adds: &quot;Subsequent Social tests in the same scene suffer a one-die penalty for you, because you come across as boastful, overbearing, dubious, or whatever\u2019s appropriate.\u200b&quot; What a weird approach to this idea...<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________<br /> <br /> And I think it should be emphasized just how bad the writing for the Project Twilight Loresheet is... oof...<br /> <br /> Like this gem:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They\u2019re not all the same thing\u2026 but they\u2019re all the same thing\u200b, ... </div> </div> </div>and this kind of repetition just keeps happening here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... if you know how to look at it. And however you look at it, ... </div> </div> </div>And you'd think it would stop because things have repeated themselves already two times but no...:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ... you\u2019ve got some dirt on the organization that you can use to influence its operations. It\u2019s really dangerous shit \u2014 whatever the reason, you\u2019ve got some sway over one ...\u200b </div> </div> </div>Whoever wrote this was either purposefully inflating the word-count without actually adding content or... I don't know... Who knows why somebody would write like this... And how did nobody else notice this...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-21T23:24:47-07:00","id":1515826,"title":"","content":"I have seen similar takes on making garou less powerful, usually from people who compare what the garou can do to what vampires can do. The problem is that garou stakes are MUCH higher and their foes are often aspects of things.<br /> <br /> Depowering garou to make them more 'balanced' never works, especially if you keep the whole warrior of gaia aspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T01:55:05-07:00","id":1515832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515826#post1515826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen similar takes on making garou less powerful, usually from people who compare what the garou can do to what vampires can do. The problem is that garou stakes are MUCH higher and their foes are often aspects of things.<br /> <br /> Depowering garou to make them more 'balanced' never works, especially if you keep the whole warrior of gaia aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It also works on the fallacy the differant creatures have to rock the same power level. unless youre running a crossover game it isnt an issue. I don't really care if my arete 4 hermetic could easily take my equivelant lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 06-22-2023, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T02:16:25-07:00","id":1515835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515826#post1515826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depowering garou to make them more 'balanced' never works, especially if you keep the whole warrior of gaia aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if in this case, they're actually deemphasizing the whole spiritual aspect of Garou and instead try to bring the game more in line with the description of werewolves in the H5 corebook:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves rampage against the structures that have elevated humanity from the poverty of the past, devoting themselves to a furious primitivism enforced by fang and claw.\u200b </div> </div> </div>So instead of focusing on a spiritual war against the Wyrm, the focus is instead on human infrastructure, industry and organisations that are considered spiritually harmful. Meanwhile, any interactions with the Umbra and spirits happen rarely and are more like a mystery to solve than some integral part of Garou life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T03:36:53-07:00","id":1515843,"title":"","content":"The 4th dot in project t. Is the worse one. It you dont buy it, then project t. Will most likely never bother your party period. If you buy it, the st need to do a backward flip to introduce p.t. threath to the party AND THEN alert the player about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T14:55:59-07:00","id":1515898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515756#post1515756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay sooo;<br /> <br /> Staying in Crinos without killing costs WP.<br /> <br /> You need to use WP to stay in the umbra or TAKE AGG DAMAGE!?<br /> <br /> There are TWO important tools made EXTREMELY unpleasant to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The spirits wilds constitute a mystery even to the garou, whose animistic outlook makes them familiar to the spirit world but not strickly of it&quot;<br /> <br /> *Caugh* what is this? It's exactly the opposite! The gaou are, by their half spirit nature, OF the spirit world as much as the material one. They are of it, but not necessarily familiar to it.<br /> <br /> And it's indeed their nature that give them a form of understanding of the umbra, not their animistic outlook, which is a consequence of the former.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The theory that the authors of W5 despise Wta seems to be more and more valid.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit, the twilight project one is indeed also weird. The V5 second inquisition loresheets were all about knowing how to avoid the SI's attention, but this one seems like garou have some interests in snitching to an org dedicated to hunt them.<br /> <br /> If anything, it should have been the reverse.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I distinctly PREDICTED that the Parawolf writers would gimp anything to do with the Umbra this edition. I knew this would happen, but I'm still somehow baffled at how bad this is.<br /> <br /> It's like the writers/developers of W5 have NEVER even played or read anything that has to do with previous Werewolf editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T15:01:21-07:00","id":1515899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515756#post1515756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay sooo;<br /> <br /> Staying in Crinos without killing costs WP.<br /> <br /> You need to use WP to stay in the umbra or TAKE AGG DAMAGE!?<br /> <br /> There are TWO important tools made EXTREMELY unpleasant to use.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The spirits wilds constitute a mystery even to the garou, whose animistic outlook makes them familiar to the spirit world but not strickly of it&quot;<br /> <br /> *Caugh* what is this? It's exactly the opposite! The gaou are, by their half spirit nature, OF the spirit world as much as the material one. They are of it, but not necessarily familiar to it.<br /> <br /> And it's indeed their nature that give them a form of understanding of the umbra, not their animistic outlook, which is a consequence of the former.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> The theory that the authors of W5 despise Wta seems to be more and more valid.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit, the twilight project one is indeed also weird. The V5 second inquisition loresheets were all about knowing how to avoid the SI's attention, but this one seems like garou have some interests in snitching to an org dedicated to hunt them.<br /> <br /> If anything, it should have been the reverse.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I distinctly PREDICTED that the Parawolf writers would gimp anything to do with the Umbra this edition. I knew this would happen, but I'm still somehow baffled at how bad this is.<br /> <br /> It's like the writers/developers of W5 have NEVER even played or read anything that has to do with previous Werewolf editions.<br /> <br /> W5 needs to be <i>stopped\u200b</i>.<br /> <br /> lol<br /> <br /> EDIT: (God, my post just got caught in the Spam dragnet just for correcting a minor spelling error. The spam filter is so aggressive. Just tell me if my duplicate comment shows up and I'll delete it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T16:44:13-07:00","id":1515910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515899#post1515899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Man, I distinctly PREDICTED that the Parawolf writers would gimp anything to do with the Umbra this edition. I knew this would happen, but I'm still somehow baffled at how bad this is.<br /> <br /> It's like the writers/developers of W5 have NEVER even played or read anything that has to do with previous Werewolf editions.<br /> <br /> W5 needs to be <i>stopped\u200b</i>.<br /> <br /> lol<br /> <br /> EDIT: (God, my post just got caught in the Spam dragnet just for correcting a minor spelling error. The spam filter is so aggressive. Just tell me if my duplicate comment shows up and I'll delete it)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem isn't that they didn't read it, but that they tagged what they read for future deletion. Similarly, they might well have played it in the past... and because it wasn't crossover friendly, ended up as a hate sink. Just another way of saying that the plan and the talent slated to orchestrate it were aggressively against pretty much everything in Apocalypse whether it deserved it (Thrall of the Wyrm, reproductive woes with non-Kitsune and non-Nagah, the worst and stereotypical sides of the tribes) or not (the Umbra, Crinos, the option to play out frenzies as a player instead of having the ST do everything... I could go on, but I'd be here for a while). It's all part of a likely aim to flatten everything to make it crossover and LARP friendly because Paradox intends to try and corner as many of the markets as possible. So, like that one story in the anthology from about ten years ago where Pentex sends a Skin Dancer to try and steal every tribe's tales for marketing fodder, only more meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T20:39:06-07:00","id":1515924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515843#post1515843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 4th dot in project t. Is the worse one. It you dont buy it, then project t. Will most likely never bother your party period. If you buy it, the st need to do a backward flip to introduce p.t. threath to the party AND THEN alert the player about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. &quot;This niche antagonist organization that isn't going to appear in your game will now appear in your game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-22T20:43:43-07:00","id":1515925,"title":"","content":"On the cost of Werewolves to stay in the Umbra I have to assume that there will be other rules or rituals to allow you to bypass that. For example, Garou who move to the High Umbra and get into one of the Realms probably shouldn't need to spend willpower or die. Or maybe there is a ritual that can be used on Garou who embark on a spirit quest that removes the need to spend willpower or die when they travel into the Umbra. I sincerely hope that the willpower/damage rule is just there for very short duration hops across the Gauntlet, more of a rule that was introduced in order to try and &quot;balance out&quot; combat capabilities of werewolves and vampires, and that werewolves will still be able to explore or spend time in the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-23T01:55:56-07:00","id":1515935,"title":"","content":"I think anything that requires WP like Gifts and Rites, Crinos-form and staying for a &quot;protracted&quot; amount of time (whatever that will end up being) in the Umbra are an issue in light of the Tribe-Bans. At the end of the day, it comes down to what sort of ST you're playing with. Things like &quot;opportunity to satisfy your curiosity&quot;, &quot;witnessing a preventable act of injustice&quot; or &quot;characters under your hospitality come to no harm&quot; aren't things a player can control. And if you trigger the Ban getting only to heal one WP next session becomes a real issue in light of all these things where the mechanic is &quot;Spend WP or a bad thing happens.&quot;. And in the same way, Touchstones expect STs to threaten/harm them in order to engage with the vulnerability of having a Touchstone, Bans expect the ST to set up scenarios where engaging in the behavior the Ban asks for is a choice with consequences. But I think there are two ways for this mechanics to stop working: One is if the consequences are so light that it isn't really that much of a big deal and the other is if you stack the deck so high against one particular choice that there really is only one choice. And I think with the high value WP has in this game, you got a case of the latter. Only regenerating 1 WP next session is so much worse because of how many mechanics are then turned against your character (dealing with Frenzy alone with an unhealed WP-track... first you have the WP-test whether a severe provocation triggers your Frenzy and then you have <i>another </i>WP-test whether you will stop killing at some point...) that then means those characters who have these behavior-specific Bans really gotta engage in that behavior no matter what.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T09:17:00-07:00","id":1516014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515935#post1515935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think anyth