con b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah<br /> Thats why such a depiciton a &quot;zombie wolf&quot; as a Talon - IF it ws a Talon - bothers me<br /> Such art would be okay if the Tribe would be a fallen tribe, or really close to it, but if they seem to be getting by just as well as GWs?<br /> Nope<br /> But this is just my two cents</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, if the concept of that wolf is in any way 'this is what wild wolves look like in W5', we have some VERY massive tonal issues at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T07:24:56-07:00","id":1516210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516205#post1516205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you link to the ks page?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf1871/werewolf-l-apocalypse.html\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25049_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25049\" data-vbnamecard=\"25049\">ZakRulz</a> refers to is a stretch-goal and these are essentially Tribe-cards or pamphlets (ran it through Google translate)...? I don't know in what format they present this but it's just each Tribe-section presented again as an extra document. The idea is that when you choose a Tribe you use that instead of opening the corebook each time. But the first example shown is the Red Talons where the four figures depicted are the two wolves, the half-naked man in the background and the woman with the dagger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T07:31:17-07:00","id":1516211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516210#post1516210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the <a href=\"https://www.gameontabletop.com/cf1871/werewolf-l-apocalypse.html\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>. What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25049_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25049\" data-vbnamecard=\"25049\">ZakRulz</a> refers to is a stretch-goal and these are essentially Tribe-cards or pamphlets (ran it through Google translate)...? I don't know in what format they present this but it's just each Tribe-section presented again as an extra document. The idea is that when you choose a Tribe you use that instead of opening the corebook each time. But the first example shown is the Red Talons where the four figures depicted are the two wolves, the half-naked man in the background and the woman with the dagger.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> So we have a military person, a naked dude, a ghostly wolf and... a mangy wolf.<br /> <br /> That is very VERY bad if they are trying to make the Talons seem convincing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T11:19:19-07:00","id":1516236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516211#post1516211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> So we have a military person, a naked dude, a ghostly wolf and... a mangy wolf.<br /> <br /> That is very VERY bad if they are trying to make the Talons seem convincing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mange wolf could be the victim of some Pentex experiments or regular human atrocities that have left it terribly scarred, which brought First Change upon the wolf; he would now be a force of vengeance against those who desecrated its forest, killed its pack and made it suffer so much. <br /> <br /> Would sound quite Talonish","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:10:47-07:00","id":1516238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516236#post1516236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mange wolf could be the victim of some Pentex experiments or regular human atrocities that have left it terribly scarred, which brought First Change upon the wolf; he would now be a force of vengeance against those who desecrated its forest, killed its pack and made it suffer so much.<br /> <br /> Would sound quite Talonish</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the best case scenario. But I'm still doubtful.<br /> <br /> Though, given how smol the wolves are, I propose a headcanon; in WoD5, there are no actual wolves left, only wolf-like pariah dogs. That way the 'looks like a big dog' makes sense and the size difference is not so silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:20:05-07:00","id":1516240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516236#post1516236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mange wolf could be the victim of some Pentex experiments or regular human atrocities that have left it terribly scarred, which brought First Change upon the wolf; he would now be a force of vengeance against those who desecrated its forest, killed its pack and made it suffer so much.<br /> <br /> Would sound quite Talonish</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that we tend to be towards the critical end of the spectrum, but I'm fascinated by how you always find something to justify it, no matter how likely it may or may not be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:29:18-07:00","id":1516241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516240#post1516240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that we tend to be towards the critical end of the spectrum, but I'm fascinated by how you always find something to justify it, no matter how likely it may or may not be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not justifying anything, I'm making guesses with your same amount of information \ud83d\ude03.<br /> <br /> Do we have any proof it's anything else? It's literally 4 example character art, without context. I think my possible explanation is no less grounded than &quot;Parawolf writers are convinced that wild wolves go around with exposed bones&quot;.<br /> <br /> I may be over optimistic? But here there is a clear tendency of going into hyperboles and take them as facts. \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 06-26-2023, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:43:23-07:00","id":1516243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516241#post1516241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not justifying anything, I'm making guesses with the same probabilitg of them being true than yours \ud83d\ude03.<br /> <br /> Do you have any proof it's anything else? It's literally 4 example character art, without context. I think my possible explanation is a bit more grounded than &quot;Parawolf writers are convinced that wild wolves go around with exposed bones&quot;.<br /> <br /> I may be over optimistic? But here there is a clear tendency of going into hyperboles and take them as facts. \ud83d\ude05</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparison of Lupus and Hispo form to dogs that are laughably small in comparison to even a typical wolf isn't exactly doing the W5 writing any favors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:53:39-07:00","id":1516245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516243#post1516243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The comparison of Lupus and Hispo form to dogs that are laughably small in comparison to even a typical wolf isn't exactly doing the W5 writing any favors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've seen some wild numbers thrown around here as well. Wolves are on average bigger than dogs, but not enormously so: they are generally longer and heavier, but not necessarily taller, they are usually smaller than Danes and a bit bigger than German Shepherds, but it also depends on the specific species.<br /> <br /> I have no doubts that to an uneducated urbanite in densely urbanized Europe or in an American metropolis, a average to small wolf would look like a big dog. Also because wolves have become very rare, at least in Europe, and only a few people have seen them outside zoos or Game of Thrones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 06-26-2023, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T13:24:32-07:00","id":1516248,"title":"","content":"The description of the forms makes no sense. The Lupus-description would make sense if there you got &quot;This looks like a really large dog.&quot;. Lighting, distance, unfamiliarity... all sorts of reasons why someone wouldn't realize what they're looking at. But with Hispo the size is comparable to horses, bears, lions... there's no mistaking that form for any kind of dog. On the other hand, if in the setting of W5 these were apt comparisons then why isn't there a permanent stealth bonus for Lupus and a removal of the Stealth-penalty for Hispo...? After all, according to the descriptions we're just talking about &quot;big&quot; and &quot;really large&quot; dogs here.<br /> <br /> They somehow managed to find the perfect middle ground between failing in two different ways...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:08:31-07:00","id":1516253,"title":"","content":"Hispo is the really dissonant thing: I suppose they have rebooted its general size to make it less overt, even I wouldn't mistake a lion-sized canine for a Dane XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:13:00-07:00","id":1516256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516245#post1516245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I've seen some wild numbers thrown around here as well. Wolves are on average bigger than dogs, but not enormously so: they are generally longer and heavier, but not necessarily taller, they are usually smaller than Danes and a bit bigger than German Shepherds, but it also depends on the specific species.<br /> <br /> I have no doubts that to an uneducated urbanite in densely urbanized Europe or in an American metropolis, a average to small wolf would look like a big dog. Also because wolves have become very rare, at least in Europe, and only a few people have seen them outside zoos or Game of Thrones.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has seen a wolf in the wild in Europe. It may be my lizard brain screaming at me because I was in the woods, but that sure didn't look like a dog to me. And while you are not likely to see them in England, Germany or Norway, they've been growing back quite steadily in the Pirnees, Balkans, Italy and the Alps. We've actually gotten to the point that while there are conservation laws for Wolves, they may even be too lenient, and there are movements to drop the numbers again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:33:46-07:00","id":1516258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1516248#post1516248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The description of the forms makes no sense. The Lupus-description would make sense if there you got &quot;This looks like a really large dog.&quot;. Lighting, distance, unfamiliarity... all sorts of reasons why someone wouldn't realize what they're looking at. But with Hispo the size is comparable to horses, bears, lions... there's no mistaking that form for any kind of dog. On the other hand, if in the setting of W5 these were apt comparisons then why isn't there a permanent stealth bonus for Lupus and a removal of the Stealth-penalty for Hispo...? After all, according to the descriptions we're just talking about &quot;big&quot; and &quot;really large&quot; dogs here.<br /> <br /> They somehow managed to find the perfect middle ground between failing in two different ways...</div> </div> </div> </div>They still walk silently i guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:52:16-07:00","id":1516514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515745-w5-loresheets?p=1515759#post1515759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Forget the war against the Wyrm, try surviving minimun-wage-labor/gig-work first!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is the meme from W5<br /> <br /> <img width=\"600\" height=\"382\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FzvAUMtWYAA8EDw?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FzvAUMtWYAA8EDw?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" data-thumb-url=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/FzvAUMtWYAA8EDw?format=jpg&amp;name=large\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10047-vis\u00e3o-de-\u00e1guia","name":"Vis\u00